ently beating all of the opponent's bluffs and lower high cards. However, you lose to any pair. Betting is unlikely to be profitable because:\n1.  Worse hands (like Q-high) will likely fold, so you gain no value.\n2.  Better hands (any pair) will likely call a small bet, causing you to lose chips.\n3.  Bluffing to make a weak pair fold is risky and high-variance for such a small pot.\n\nChecking back is the dominant strategy here to realize your equity. You will win the pot if the opponent has a weaker high card, which is consistent with their passive play.\n\nReason:\nYou have the strongest possible High Card hand (Ace-King). The opponent has shown weakness by checking four times. Betting yields little value as worse hands fold and better hands call. Checking guarantees a showdown where you likely win against their missed draws or lower high cards without risking more chips.\n\nAnswer: 0"}
