ich would force you to fold or commit more chips with a weak hand, endangering your lead. Checking allows you to control the pot size, see the River card for free, and potentially win at showdown without additional risk.\n\nReason: You have a weak made hand (bottom pair) and are protecting an overall tournament lead in the last hand. The opponent has shown passivity. Checking is the safest play to keep the pot small and avoid unnecessary losses, which aligns with the goal of maintaining your chip advantage to win the game.\n\nAnswer: 0'}
